  "details": "Build number:1866 (2026.2.3p2)\n\nSummary:\n\nWhen attaching an image to an Invite using the VRC+ feature, a photo taken on the spot attaches and displays correctly, but an existing photo selected from the photo gallery is not reflected/applied.\n\nNote: The 2026.1.2 Open Beta (Build 1797) patch notes include \"Fixed VRC+ image attachment dialogue for invites and replies,\" but this issue still occurs on Build 1866, so this may be a regression or an incomplete fix.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Open the Invite menu and choose to attach an image (VRC+).\n\n2. Select an existing photo from the photo gallery and send the Invite.\n\n3. The attached image is not applied to the Invite.\n\n(For comparison: taking a new photo on the spot and attaching it works correctly.)\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nA photo selected from the gallery should attach and display correctly on the Invite.\n\nActual behavior:\n\nThe gallery photo is not reflected/applied. Only freshly taken photos work.\n\nEnvironments tested (issue reproduced in all of the following):\n\n- Live build (Build 1866)\n\n- Open Beta (Build 1866)\n\n- Unity 6 build\n\nReceiver side verified:\n\nThe missing image was confirmed on the recipient's side both in-game and in the web browser (vrchat.com notifications), so this does not appear to be a display issue limited to a specific client.",
